# gatekeeper-__slug__

**Status: scaffold.** Generated by `pnpm gatekeepers:scaffold __slug__`. It runs against a synthetic
fake provider (`src/fake-provider.ts`) through a typed client stub (`src/client.ts`). Nothing here has
been reviewed, and nothing talks to a real __title__. Scaffolding never marks a connector ready:
`connection.json`'s `status` stays `scaffold` until a person moves it on.

| Status | Meaning | Where it runs |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `scaffold` | Generated, not reviewed | Local development, when selected explicitly |
| `conformant` | Agent-facing contract reviewed; the shared conformance suite passes against the fake provider | Local development, when selected explicitly |
| `reference` | Reviewed against a real provider contract | Releases; the default selection |
| `production` | Accepted live | Releases; the default selection |

## Layout

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `src/__slug__.ts` | Vendor, account, verifier, the collection gatekeeper and the agent's session |
| `src/types.d.ts` | The agent-facing contract. Review it before anything else |
| `src/client.ts` | SCAFFOLD client stub: one named method per provider call, never a generic proxy |
| `src/fake-provider.ts` | Synthetic data source: revisions, idempotency keys and revocation enforced |
| `__tests__/conformance-adapter.ts` | Maps the shared conformance suite onto this gatekeeper |
| `connection.json` | The package contract, validated by `scripts/connection-package.schema.json` |

## Develop

__DEVELOP__

## From scaffold to connector

1. Rename the resource kind, session and methods to the provider's domain in `src/types.d.ts`, and
   review that contract before implementing it.
2. Replace `src/client.ts`'s fake with the provider's API. Classify every call as a read or a write
   in `connection.json`, and list every provider error with whether a retry can succeed.
3. Keep the fake provider for tests, and keep the conformance adapter passing every case; record any
   case that cannot be expressed under `conformance.perConnector` with its reason.
4. Name every configuration value the package reads under `credentials` (names only, never values).
5. Fill in the SOP below, then ask a reviewer to advance `status`.

